6-10-08T18:22:30.193Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7794387?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gkrajniak","id":7794387,"login":"gkrajniak","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3OTQzODc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmfp/openmfp.org/commits/0fae5c439a353c2ba3d009924e7c954a932b8ec3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:06:46Z","email":"gkrajniak@gmail.com","name":"Grzegorz Krajniak"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T10:06:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deps): resolve npm audit and Dependabot vulnerabilities (#137)\n\n* fix(deps): resolve npm audit and Dependabot vulnerabilities\n\n## Summary\n\nResolves the fixable `npm audit` findings and Dependabot alerts. Only `package-lock.json` changes.\n\n## Lockfile updates (`npm audit fix`)\n\n- vue and @vue/* 3.5.21 → 3.5.43 (@vue/server-renderer advisory)\n- dompurify 3.4.13 → 3.4.16\n- source-map-js 1.2.1 → 1.2.2\n- postcss 8.5.26 → 8.5.29, nanoid 3.3.18 → 3.3.20 and related Babel/Vue compiler packages within their ranges\n\n## Not fixable without a major upgrade (dev only, build tooling)\n\n- vite 5.4.21 (GHSA-fx2h-pf6j-xcff, GHSA-v6wh-96g9-6wx3, GHSA-4w7w-66w2-5vf9) and esbuild 0.21.5 (GHSA-67mh-4wv8-2f99): vitepress 1.6.4 (latest stable) requires vite `^5.4.14`; the fixes are in vite 6.4.3 and esbuild 0.25.0, which only vitepress 2 (alpha) supports\n- katex 0.16.47 (GHSA-238p-pmpm-9mq7, low): fixed in 0.18.2; mermaid 11.16.1 requires katex `^0.16.45`\n\n## Verification\n\n`npm ci`, `npm install` and `npm run build` pass. The repository has no tests.\n\nOn-behalf-of: @SAP grzegorz.krajniak@sap.com\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>\n\n* fix(deps): override vite to 6.4.3\n\n## Override\n\n- vite 5.4.21 → 6.4.3 via `overrides`; vitepress 1.6.4 requires vite `^5.4.14`, and the fix is only in vite 6.4.3. This also moves esbuild 0.21.5 → 0.25.12.\n\n## Verification\n\n`npm ci`, `npm install` and `npm run build` pass.\n\nOn-behalf-of: @SAP grzegorz.krajniak@sap.com\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"0e82a893a9a7d3e73f65072dd5b42c43c05d50a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmfp/openmfp.org/git/trees/0e82a893a9a7d3e73f65072dd5b42c43c05d50a4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmfp/openmfp.org/git/commits/0fae5c439a353c2ba3d009924e7c954a932b8ec3","verification":{"payload":"tree 0e82a893a9a7d3e73f65072dd5b42c43c05d50a4\nparent 05e9df4151ca9ed5b56e8534e7d360a01f0c15b8\nauthor Grzegorz Krajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com> 1791367606 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791367606 +0200\n\nfix(deps): resolve npm audit and Dependabot vulnerabilities (#137)\n\n* fix(deps): resolve npm audit and Dependabot vulnerabilities\n\n## Summary\n\nResolves the fixable `npm audit` findings and Dependabot alerts. Only `package-lock.json` changes.\n\n## Lockfile updates (`npm audit fix`)\n\n- vue and @vue/* 3.5.21 → 3.5.43 (@vue/server-renderer advisory)\n- dompurify 3.4.13 → 3.4.16\n- source-map-js 1.2.1 → 1.2.2\n- postcss 8.5.26 → 8.5.29, nanoid 3.3.18 → 3.3.20 and related Babel/Vue compiler packages within their ranges\n\n## Not fixable without a major upgrade (dev only, build tooling)\n\n- vite 5.4.21 (GHSA-fx2h-pf6j-xcff, GHSA-v6wh-96g9-6wx3, GHSA-4w7w-66w2-5vf9) and esbuild 0.21.5 (GHSA-67mh-4wv8-2f99): vitepress 1.6.4 (latest stable) requires vite `^5.4.14`; the fixes are in vite 6.4.3 and esbuild 0.25.0, which only vitepress 2 (alpha) supports\n- katex 0.16.47 (GHSA-238p-pmpm-9mq7, low): fixed in 0.18.2; mermaid 11.16.1 requires katex `^0.16.45`\n\n## Verification\n\n`npm ci`, `npm install` and `npm run build` pass. The repository has no tests.\n\nOn-behalf-of: @SAP grzegorz.krajniak@sap.com\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>\n\n* fix(deps): override vite to 6.4.3\n\n## Override\n\n- vite 5.4.21 → 6.4.3 via `overrides`; vitepress 1.6.4 requires vite `^5.4.14`, and the fix is only in vite 6.4.3. This also moves esbuild 0.21.5 → 0.25.12.\n\n## Verification\n\n`npm ci`, `npm install` and `npm run build` pass.\n\nOn-behalf-of: @SAP grzegorz.krajniak@sap.com\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxhm2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtoQQAHj5e9Yd/67QFzgFdXOlSRly\n0YMR+h4EEBckgPlwg35y2wjYScBNhiHgIgyoxT0b7IJO7dinU2k3nVjtGGXnuWWG\nf3sUaNRWfK4TNhkHRDStHGnYVYOSLF1PSIW0GX7jzg+XoZPPye93OhFrRP0aX0nT\nblJG33vrgrELQ0HWuAD296BkqhzDHh/urscQlHMoUy0944ZzaiBBZpdV4vRPgq0t\nc7J7UKtUvsU/l3/6jq/0j8aE8B4RFQhWZH7cU+TnYbouVxOvub0j55RqU3/whFHj\nhEW4VoaBT7rL8Piq5XasMutR0wHK6qCVg0MJIJsm9T9IUxKtGufm/1++BnWMzpnf\nxCeWLomVc2Xdze552RDwhZ20/edlYJVKSsG+wmxWjXcfFieMy/2GTiZmFa8UWtS5\noRENoF40Zom+v0ZUPtU7ybjJeIQyeU/ZO1WI4FdATRg+3d1NDV2v0SHaAeasGgU4\nOJzoCoz/hi8MbW3lBdH+ZXslMwQwV29iDtfQbBAPvY2jqXsGgpAsCV9UmbOSNRnC\n4VJ7myaJjbzsWduusma2iD/1wsF2swbA9zqeuULOiMQAEQxy61UYJ67hUM6QYzFB\n8/juIc/93/RbmotzkPBU59ASPK0JUbL15fOl0SBaW4EdpYt6F3XlG6d61rV8dALf\nPNwxlPuEN5zkRow5/pyu\n=cXN9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T10:06:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmfp/openmfp.org/commit/0fae5c439a353c2ba3d009924e7c954a932b8ec3","node_id":"C_kwDOLsv8uNoAKDBmYWU1YzQzOWEzNTNjMmJhM2QwMDk5MjRlN2M5NTRhOTMyYjhlYzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmfp/openmfp.org/commit/05e9df4151ca9ed5b56e8534e7d360a01f0c15b8","sha":"05e9df4151ca9ed5b56e8534e7d360a01f0c15b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmfp/openmfp.org/commits/05e9df4151ca9ed5b56e8534e7d360a01f0c15b8"}],"sha":"0fae5c439a353c2ba3d009924e7c954a932b8ec3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmfp/openmfp.org/commits/0fae5c439a353c2ba3d009924e7c954a932b8ec3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7794387?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gkrajniak","id":7794387,"login":"gkrajniak","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3OTQzODc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkrajniak","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmfp/openmfp.org/commits/05e9df4151ca9ed5b56e8534e7d360a01f0c15b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T12:39:45Z","email":"gkrajniak@gmail.com","name":"Grzegorz Krajniak"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T12:39:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: patch dependency vulnerabilities (16 → 4 dev-only) (#133)\n\nResolve the fixable npm audit findings pulled through mermaid and\nvitepress-plugin-mermaid:\n\n- bump mermaid 11.13.0 → 11.16.1 (HTML/CSS injection, prototype\n  pollution, and infinite-loop DoS advisories)\n- npm audit fix updates the transitive tree: dompurify, postcss,\n  preact, rollup, nanoid, lodash-es (chevrotain chain), uuid, etc.\n\nnpm audit: 16 vulnerabilities (11 high, 5 moderate) → 4 (1 high,\n3 moderate).\n\nThe remaining 4 all trace to a single root: vitepress 1.6.4 (the latest\nstable) pins vite 5 / esbuild 0.21, pulling dev-server/build-time\nadvisories (esbuild dev-server SSRF, vite `.map` path traversal, and the\nWindows-only `server.fs.deny` bypass and launch-editor NTLM disclosure).\nThe patched vite (>6.4.2) is only available via a vitepress 2.x\npre-release, so there is no non-breaking fix. These affect only the\nvite/esbuild dev server; this is a static site built with `vitepress\nbuild` and deployed to gh-pages, so the dev server never runs in\nproduction. Deferred pending a vitepress major upgrade.\n\nVerified: vitepress build completes successfully.\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"c3feb84d0f7521512662dd2e9178b8a8357724a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmfp/openmfp.org/git/trees/c3feb84d0f7521512662dd2e9178b8a8357724a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmfp/openmfp.org/git/commits/05e9df4151ca9ed5b56e8534e7d360a01f0c15b8","verification":{"payload":"tree c3feb84d0f7521512662dd2e9178b8a8357724a3\nparent cfb81664dff4f6a77fb09d36d3a2472f089eb973\nauthor Grzegorz Krajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com> 1786711185 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786711185 +0200\n\nfix: patch dependency vulnerabilities (16 → 4 dev-only) (#133)\n\nResolve the fixable npm audit findings pulled through mermaid and\nvitepress-plugin-mermaid:\n\n- bump mermaid 11.13.0 → 11.16.1 (HTML/CSS injection, prototype\n  pollution, and infinite-loop DoS advisories)\n- npm audit fix updates the transitive tree: dompurify, postcss,\n  preact, rollup, nanoid, lodash-es (chevrotain chain), uuid, etc.\n\nnpm audit: 16 vulnerabilities (11 high, 5 moderate) → 4 (1 high,\n3 moderate).\n\nThe remaining 4 all trace to a single root: vitepress 1.6.4 (the latest\nstable) pins vite 5 / esbuild 0.21, pulling dev-server/build-time\nadvisories (esbuild dev-server SSRF, vite `.map` path traversal, and the\nWindows-only `server.fs.deny` bypass and launch-editor NTLM disclosure).\nThe patched vite (>6.4.2) is only available via a vitepress 2.x\npre-release, so there is no non-breaking fix. These affect only the\nvite/esbuild dev server; this is a static site built with `vitepress\nbuild` and deployed to gh-pages, so the dev server never runs in\nproduction. Deferred pending a vitepress major upgrade.\n\nVerified: vitepress build completes successfully.\n\nSigned-off-by: gkrajniak <gkrajniak@gmail.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfwyRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASzIQAKGWmzP3B0JlaFYVdCCrmGAE\njGeLWu6kxdKdKaa5I3SIjmA0O8mbwgMKZoqZWEBK0VdX+gBX5SSotJhlYc+WBDxg\naRZa/7sVJpZeMJkE5C7BAl